	Section:
		Text: Layers and rotation
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Rotation when painting
		Paragraph: A rotated `Frame`, `Overlay` or `Page overlay` takes up its place as if it were not rotated: the rotation only changes how it is painted. It suits what goes on top of everything, such as a stamp.
			Style: intro
		Text: Overlay with Rotate: -12 in the top right corner of a Frame
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Style: stage
			Paragraph: Quote 2026-014 for the kitchen on Calle Mayor: six walnut chairs, one dining table and the delivery to the second floor.
			Overlay:
				Offset: 50 20 auto auto
				Rotate: -12
				Text: DRAFT
					Style: stamp
		Text: Frame with Rotate: 3: its siblings keep their place
			Style: label
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 16 0
		Frame:
			Rotate: 3
			Box:
				Padding: 10
				Background: tint
				Border: 1
				Border color: accent
			Paragraph: This frame is tilted when painted, but the paragraph below starts where it would start without the rotation.
				Box:
					Margin: 0
		Paragraph: The next paragraph, in its unrotated place.
			Box:
				Margin: 20 0 0 0
